From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 8 May 2026 20:18:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: bounds-check RtlIsEcCode against non-canonical
 pointers

The inlined bitmap probe in callers like virtual_unwind segfaults when
called with a corrupted unwind context (e.g. context->Pc set to
0xffffffff00000000). Real Windows sizes EcCodeBitMap for the canonical
48-bit user-space range; out-of-range or non-canonical pointers should
return FALSE rather than walking past the end of the bitmap allocation.

Add a bounds check on ptr (>= 0x800000000000) and a NULL bitmap guard.
The compiler inlines this into all RtlIsEcCode call sites (including
virtual_unwind, RtlUnwindEx, etc.), so any corrupted-context recovery
path is now safe.

(cherry picked from commit 5ec17759cdff6370ae31668eb4f08b54794d57af)
Madeira-commit: ac650deca36b8ac969bffad0c5076725fb5c52b5
Rebased: clean
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-wine-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
index ae1cb52..1aa6734 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
@@ -1570,6 +1570,10 @@ BOOLEAN WINAPI RtlIsEcCode( ULONG_PTR ptr )
 {
     const UINT64 *map = (const UINT64 *)NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->EcCodeBitMap;
     ULONG_PTR page = ptr / page_size;
+    /* The EcCodeBitMap covers only the canonical 48-bit user-space range. Querying
+       a non-canonical / corrupted pointer (e.g. from a damaged unwind context) must
+       not segfault — return FALSE for any pointer the bitmap can't represent. */
+    if (!map || ptr >= 0x800000000000ULL) return FALSE;
     return (map[page / 64] >> (page & 63)) & 1;
 }
 
